// case: generic-model-constrained-type-parameter
// what: `model Box[T: int]` promises something about the argument and this
//      compiler is not in a position to keep it -- the argument is INFERRED, so
//      there is nothing to check a constraint against. parseGenericParams
//      parses one for `fn` and `trait`, where an unimplemented constraint costs
//      nothing because a parameter type is not lowered from there; a model field
//      IS lowered, so accepting one would be accepting a promise about a value
//      nobody supplies.
//
//      Note what is refused: the constraint, not the parameter. `model Box[T]`
//      is real (n47 is the shape that is still refused, and why).
// expect-error: 'model Box[T: int]' is not supported: a model's type parameter is inferred from the value written for it
model Box[T: int] {
    v: T
}

fn main() -> int {
    val b = Box { v: 1 }
    print(b.v)
    return 0
}